--- A function copied per signature is scanned in its own scope, as the
--- function itself is: its first assignment to a name is a local of its
--- own, whatever the program's top level holds under the name, and inside
--- a standard module's copy the program's names are invisible. The copy
--- of llm's `act` made for a second tool list had read the program's
--- `one` — the record the first call answered — as the loop's own local
--- `one` (a schema's text), and refused the module's own push onto its
--- list in both modes. Here a function of the program's, copied for
--- lists of ints, floats and text, and web.auth's `sign`, copied for a
--- map and a parsed value, each assign a local named like a value of the
--- program's top level of another kind. (The loop moved to its own
--- repository with llm, 2026-11-07.)
use web, web.auth

--- the items as text, joined
fn shown[xs]
    lines = []
    for x in xs
        one = str[x]
        lines = push[lines, one]
    return join[lines, ', ']

one = len[shown[[1, 2]]]
log[one]
log[shown[[1.5, 2.5]]]
log[shown[['a', 'b']]]

secret = 'a-secret-of-at-least-thirty-two-chars'
written = 0
payload = [1, 2]
first = sign[map[user = 'ada'], secret]
second = sign[json['{"user": "bob"}'], secret]
log[len[split[first, '.']]]
log[str[verify[second, secret].user]]
log[written]
log[len[payload]]
